@startuml habit-service-class-diagram
title Level 3: Code - Class Diagram (habit-service) - FR-13\nOwner: Mostafa Khamis Abozead
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #555555
  BackgroundColor<<component>> #D5EFE0
  BorderColor<<component>> #2E8B57
}
skinparam interface {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #555555
}
hide empty members

legend right
  |<#D5EFE0>   | Class of a component |
  |<#FFFFFF>   | Interface / domain class |
  | Solid arrow, open head | Uses (required interface / class) |
  | Dotted arrow, hollow head | Implements (provided interface) |
  | Filled diamond | Composition |
  | Plain line | Association |
endlegend

interface IHabit <<provided>> {
  +CreateHabitAsync(studentId, request): ServiceResult<Habit>
  +CompleteHabitAsync(habitId, date): ServiceResult<Habit>
  +GetHabitsAsync(studentId): List<Habit>
  +GetStreaksAsync(studentId, today): List<HabitStreakResponse>
  +LinkToGoalAsync(habitId, goalId): ServiceResult<Habit>
}

class HabitService <<component>> {
  -repository: IHabitRepository
  --
  +CreateHabitAsync(...)
  +CompleteHabitAsync(...) / GetHabitsAsync(...)
  +GetStreaksAsync(...) / LinkToGoalAsync(...)
}

interface IHabitRepository <<required - Database>> {
  +GetHabitAsync(habitId): Task<Habit?>
  +GetHabitsByStudentAsync(studentId): Task<List<Habit>>
  +GetLogAsync(habitId, date): Task<HabitLog?>
  +GetLogsAsync(habitId): Task<List<HabitLog>>
  +AddHabitAsync(habit): Task
  +AddLogAsync(log): Task
  +SaveChangesAsync(): Task
}

class HabitRepository <<component>> {
  -context: HabitDbContext
  --
  +GetHabitAsync(...) / GetHabitsByStudentAsync(...)
  +GetLogAsync(...) / GetLogsAsync(...)
  +AddHabitAsync(...) / AddLogAsync(...)
  +SaveChangesAsync()
}

class HabitDbContext {
  +Habits: DbSet<Habit>
  +HabitLogs: DbSet<HabitLog>
}

class Habit {
  -habitId: String
  -studentId: String
  -goalId: String?
  -name: String
  -frequency: HabitFrequency
  -reminderTime: TimeOnly?
  -currentStreak: int
  -isActive: bool
}
class HabitLog {
  -logId: String
  -habitId: String
  -logDate: DateOnly
  -completed: bool
}
enum HabitFrequency {
  Daily
  Weekly
}

IHabit <|.. HabitService
HabitService --> IHabitRepository
HabitRepository ..|> IHabitRepository
HabitRepository --> HabitDbContext
HabitDbContext --> Habit
HabitDbContext --> HabitLog
Habit *-- "0..*" HabitLog
Habit --> HabitFrequency
note bottom of HabitService
SOLID applied:
S - HabitService owns streak rules; HabitRepository persists; HabitDbContext maps.
O - new behaviour is added by new implementations, not by editing HabitService.
L - HabitService can replace any other IHabit implementation.
I - IHabit exposes only the operations its clients use.
D - HabitService depends on IHabitRepository, not on HabitRepository.
end note
@enduml
